From 28280aa19c786ad457617fe66b1c66abdccd5301 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daehyun Kim <kimdhyungg@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:46:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [CBRD-27237] Probe: option C current-record guard in the
 forward-walk (local only)

Throwaway prototype of fix option C, to measure it against the probes.
Not a fix. Before deleting the chains named by an undo image, the
forward-walk reads the record now stored at the log record's slot,
follows REC_RELOCATION to REC_NEWHOME, and keeps every chain whose head
OID that record still references. A REC_BIGONE record keeps all chains.

The row identity is the slot the notify-vacuum log record names: the
home slot for heap_update_home and update_old_home, the forward slot
for update_old_forward and RVHF_DELETE_NEWHOME_NOTIFY_VACUUM.

Latch order: heap pages are read-latched one at a time and released
before the delete sysop starts, so no heap latch is held together with
an OOS latch. The record can change after the latch is released.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VC8p7DEh6NxSFKB6FVM3Nb
---
